<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Buddhist Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 4th century BCE</span> · Also known as Council of Vaishali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Buddhist Council was an assembly of monks held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishali">Vaishali</a>, according to Buddhist tradition about a century after the death of the Buddha. It was called to judge ten practices of the monks of Vaishali, among them accepting gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>, which the elders condemned as breaches of monastic discipline. Later accounts link it with the first split of the Buddhist community into the Sthavira and Mahasanghika schools.</p></div>
